<title>USA: Inglewood, Calif., city manager resigns over arena.</title>
<headline>Inglewood, Calif., city manager resigns over arena.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Inglewood, Calif., City Manager Paul Eckles announced he will step down April 1, according to a published report Thursday.</p>
<p>Eckles said his departure was prompted in part by Inglewood's failed bid to build a state-of-the-art sports arena, the Los Angeles Times reported.</p>
<p>Last week, arena developers announced that they would concentrate their efforts on building the proposed sports complex in downtown Los Angeles instead.</p>
<p>&quot;This is a deep disappointment for me and most people in the city of Inglewood,&quot; Eckles told the Times. &quot;My personal commitment to these negotiations is one of the key things that has been holding me here.&quot;</p>
